{
  "slug": "artist:krafty-kuts",
  "name": "Krafty Kuts",
  "editorial_article": "Born Martin Reeves in Bognor Regis, the English DJ and producer Krafty Kuts earned his reputation as a pioneer in the breakbeat and nu skool breaks scenes. His 2006 debut solo album, Freakshow, arrived on his own Against The Grain label and featured contributions from Tim Deluxe and Ashley Slater. Prior to this, Reeves achieved widespread recognition for his collaborative album Tricka Technology, recorded alongside fellow DJ A Skillz. His work often blends elements of funk, hip hop, and house, reflecting a career spanning nearly three decades. In 2010, his double mix CD Against the Grain received the Best Compilation award at the Breakspoll ceremony, where he also claimed the Best DJ title. His extensive production catalog includes projects like the 2017 collaboration All 4 Corners with Dynamite MC, consistently pushing his signature high-energy dance aesthetic across international festival circuits.",
